; ..\BSW364\Can\Implementation\Can.c	  6202       Once CCCR[INIT] has been cleared by the CPU, the device will then wait for 129 occurrences of Bus Idle 
; ..\BSW364\Can\Implementation\Can.c	  6203       (129 x 11 consecutive recessive bits) before resuming normal operation. 
; ..\BSW364\Can\Implementation\Can.c	  6204       At the end of the Bus_Off recovery sequence, the Error Management Counters will be reset. 
; ..\BSW364\Can\Implementation\Can.c	  6205       During the waiting time after the resetting of CCCR[INIT], each time a sequence of 11 recessive bits has been monitored, 
; ..\BSW364\Can\Implementation\Can.c	  6206       a Bit 0 Error code is written to PSR[LEC], enabling the CPU to readily check up whether the CAN bus is stuck at dominant or continuously disturbed 
; ..\BSW364\Can\Implementation\Can.c	  6207       and to monitor the Bus_Off recovery sequence. ECR[REC] is used to count these sequences. */
