; ..\BSW364\Can\Implementation\Can.c	 11989  \CM CM_CAN_HL01 A runtime check ensures controller index is always smaller than number of elements in arrays with controller amount as dimension (Qualified use-case CSL01 of ComStackLib size of ControllerData).
; ..\BSW364\Can\Implementation\Can.c	 11990  \CM CM_CAN_HL02 Qualified use-case CSL03 of ComStackLib (CanMailbox.ControllerConfigIdx is always in range of controller ControllerData)
; ..\BSW364\Can\Implementation\Can.c	 11991  \CM CM_CAN_HL03 A runtime check ensures activeSendObject index is in valid range for Can_ActiveSendObject table (Qualified use-case CSL01 of ComStackLib - Can_ActiveSendObject size is extended by CAN_MULTIPLEXED_TX_MAX within generator to allow an access to logObjHandle+CAN_MULTIPLEXED_TX_MAX).
; ..\BSW364\Can\Implementation\Can.c	 11992  \CM CM_CAN_HL17 A runtime check ensures DLC index is always smaller than the dimension of CanRxQueueBuffer.data.
; ..\BSW364\Can\Implementation\Can.c	 11993  \CM CM_CAN_HL18 A runtime check ensures HRH values is always in range of start stop index of the given mailbox type. (Qualified use-case CSL03 of ComStackLib - start-stop index fit to mailbox entrys)
; ..\BSW364\Can\Implementation\Can.c	 11994  \CM CM_CAN_HL20 A runtime check ensures size of ActiveSendData (dataByte). For CAN-FD it is checked against the size of the table. For none CAN-FD size is checked against 8 as defined.
; ..\BSW364\Can\Implementation\Can.c	 11995  \CM CM_CAN_HL22 A runtime check ensures source index for LoopTimeout array is always smaller than the dimension of LoopTimeout.
; ..\BSW364\Can\Implementation\Can.c	 11996  \CM CM_CAN_HL24 A runtime check ensures RxQueue write index is always smaller than the dimension of RxQueue (Qualified use-case CSL01 of ComStackLib).
; ..\BSW364\Can\Implementation\Can.c	 11997  \CM CM_CAN_HL25 A runtime check ensures RxQueue read index is always smaller than the dimension of RxQueue (Qualified use-case CSL01 of ComStackLib).
; ..\BSW364\Can\Implementation\Can.c	 11998  \CM CM_CAN_HL28 A runtime check ensures htrh index is always smaller than the dimension of CanMailboxState (Qualified use-case CSL01 of ComStackLib).
; ..\BSW364\Can\Implementation\Can.c	 11999  \CM CM_CAN_HL29 Qualified use-case CSL02 of ComStackLib (size of CanMailboxState == size of CanMailbox) 
; ..\BSW364\Can\Implementation\Can.c	 12000  \CM CM_CAN_HL30 Qualified use-case CSL03 of ComStackLib (CanMailbox - CanController Start/Stop HtrhIndex).
; ..\BSW364\Can\Implementation\Can.c	 12001  \CM CM_CAN_HL31 valid mailbox data area is assigned to rxStruct.pChipData pointer (Has to be given by LL implementation part).
; ..\BSW364\Can\Implementation\Can.c	 12002  \CM CM_CAN_HL32 A runtime check ensures TxHwFifo index is always smaller than the dimension of TxHwFifo (Qualified use-case CSL01 of ComStackLib).
; ..\BSW364\Can\Implementation\Can.c	 12003  \CM CM_CAN_HL33 canPdu.length is limited to size of canPdu.sdu.
; ..\BSW364\Can\Implementation\Can.c	 12004  
; ..\BSW364\Can\Implementation\Can.c	 12005  
; ..\BSW364\Can\Implementation\Can.c	 12006  \CM CM_CAN_LL_100 A runtime check ensures that the controller index is always smaller than number of elements in base address array (Qualified use-case CSL01 of ComStackLib size of ControllerData).
; ..\BSW364\Can\Implementation\Can.c	 12007  \CM CM_CAN_LL_102 A runtime check ensures controller index is always smaller than the number of elements in arrays using controller amount as dimension (Qualified use-case CSL01 of ComStackLib size of ControllerData).
; ..\BSW364\Can\Implementation\Can.c	 12008  \CM CM_CAN_LL_103 A runtime check ensures pointer access is always in the correct memory area.
; ..\BSW364\Can\Implementation\Can.c	 12009  \CM CM_CAN_LL_104 Using the bit operator "&" assures the maximum length of the index to guarantee that the dimension is sufficient.
; ..\BSW364\Can\Implementation\Can.c	 12010  \CM CM_CAN_LL_105 The loop end condition guarantees that the dimension is sufficient.
; ..\BSW364\Can\Implementation\Can.c	 12011  \CM CM_CAN_LL_107 The limited index ('0' or '1') guarantees that the dimension is sufficient.
; ..\BSW364\Can\Implementation\Can.c	 12012  \CM CM_CAN_LL_109 The static structure(element) address is assured via a fix typedef and thus always valid.
; ..\BSW364\Can\Implementation\Can.c	 12013  \CM CM_CAN_LL_111 A runtime check ensures that the channel parameter is always in the correct range.
; ..\BSW364\Can\Implementation\Can.c	 12014  \CM CM_CAN_LL_112 A runtime check ensures that the generated table has the correct size (Qualified use-case CSL01 of ComStackLib size of Can_ShmAdr).
